  "worked_solution": "Since $2,$ $3,$ and $7$ are coprime, then according to the Chinese remainder theorem, the system has a unique solution modulo $2\\cdot 3\\cdot 7=42.$\n\nWe will solve the system in two steps.\n\n**Step 1.** Find the common solution for the first and second congruences of the system.\n\nFrom the first congruence, we get\n\n$$\nx≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\,⟹\\,x=1+2t,\\,t\\in Z.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second congruence, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡2 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,3) \\\\ 1+2t & ≡2 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,3) \\\\ 2t & ≡1 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $3$ is a relatively small modulus, we can solve it by trial and error. We have that $2\\cdot 2≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3).$ So, we multiply both sides by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2t & ≡1 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,3) \\\\ 2\\cdot 2t & ≡2 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,3) \\\\ t & ≡2 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $t=2+3s,$ where $s\\in Z.$ Substituting this into the expression for $x,$ we get the common solution for the first and second congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =1+2t \\\\  & =1+2(2+3s) \\\\  & =5+6s\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2.** Find the common solution of all three congruences.\n\nNow, substituting the common solution of the first two congruences into the third congruence, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡5 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\ 5+6s & ≡5 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\ 6s & ≡0 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $7$ is a relatively small modulus, by trial and error, we have that $6\\cdot 6≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6s & ≡0 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\ 6\\cdot 6s & ≡0 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\ s & ≡0 &  & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $s=7u,$ where $u\\in Z.$ Substituting this into the expression for the common solution of the first two congruences, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5+6s \\\\  & =5+6(7u) \\\\  & =5+42u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x≡5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,42)$ is the unique solution modulo $42,$ and $x=5$ is the smallest natural number solution to the system.",
